    "summary": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-maplibre/releases/tag/0.1a0\">datasette-maplibre 0.1a0</a></p> <p>The first new Datasette geospatial plugin in quite a while! This one combines the excellent <a href=\"https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/\">MapLibre GL</a> library with <a href=\"https://openfreemap.org\">OpenFreeMap</a>, the free vector map server operated by Zsolt Ero (you should <a href=\"https://github.com/sponsors/hyperknot\">sponsor Zsolt on GitHub</",
    "body": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-maplibre/releases/tag/0.1a0\">datasette-maplibre 0.1a0</a></p> <p>The first new Datasette geospatial plugin in quite a while! This one combines the excellent <a href=\"https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/\">MapLibre GL</a> library with <a href=\"https://openfreemap.org\">OpenFreeMap</a>, the free vector map server operated by Zsolt Ero (you should <a href=\"https://github.com/sponsors/hyperknot\">sponsor Zsolt on GitHub</a>.)</p> <p>I built most of this with a single prompt to Claude Fable 5.2:</p> <blockquote> <p><code>Look at datasette-cluster-map and datasette-leaflet-geojson plugins, then look at ~/dev/tools/openfreemap-demo.html - then build a brand new Datasette plugin that uses maplibreGL and openfreemap and ",
    "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/15/datasette-maplibre/",
