    "title": "datasette 1.0a43",
    "summary": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/releases/tag/1.0a43\">datasette 1.0a43</a></p> <p>I've been leaning hard into Claude Fable 5.2 to help knock things off the <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/milestone/37\">1.0 milestone</a>, which is now 53% complete.</p> <p>The biggest 1.0 item in this release is <a href=\"https://docs.datasette.io/en/latest/plugin_hooks.html#plugin-register-output-renderer-streaming\">streaming support for output renderers</a> - ",
    "body": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/releases/tag/1.0a43\">datasette 1.0a43</a></p> <p>I've been leaning hard into Claude Fable 5.2 to help knock things off the <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/milestone/37\">1.0 milestone</a>, which is now 53% complete.</p> <p>The biggest 1.0 item in this release is <a href=\"https://docs.datasette.io/en/latest/plugin_hooks.html#plugin-register-output-renderer-streaming\">streaming support for output renderers</a> - the built-in TSV and CSV export mechanisms now use this as well, and plugins can register themselves as capable of streaming every row in a table in one go via the new <a href=\"https://docs.datasette.io/en/latest/internals.html#internals-response-stream\">Response.stream()</a> method.</p> <p>There ar",
